      "writtenOn": "2015-08-01T01:57:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "similar to what board_set_active_charge_port() does, it might be better to let USB_CHG task send the i2c transaction. so, instead of calling this function directly, you could call a board_ function that sets typec_power_path and then wakes the task.\n\nthen, if the battery is holding the bus, we won\u0027t be delaying the PD task. probably doesn\u0027t matter for dual-role toggling calls to pd_set_host_mode(), but could affect the power swap calls to pd_set_host_mode().",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
